  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A rock of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4.0\"></span> kg is thrown vertically downwards into a lake at an initial speed of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"10\"></span> m s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span>. After travelling <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"50\"></span> m, the rock hits the bottom of the lake with a speed of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"30\"></span> m s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span>. What is the kinetic energy lost by the rock because of the resistive friction force that arises due to the water in the lake?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"400\"></span> J</li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"800\"></span> J</li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4000\"></span> J</li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"8000\"></span> J</li>\n</ol>"
